data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:21:48.293232+00:00", "content": "Based on my investigation of **ce_branch24**, here's the evidence-based assessment:\n\n## Device Health Summary\n**Hardware telemetry is normal** \u2014 fan 3000 RPM, power ~72.5 W, PSU 11.88 V, temperature 29 \u00b0C [metrics:0][metrics:1][metrics:2][metrics:3]. No hardware alarms.\n\n## SD-WAN Tunnel Quality \u2014 **Degraded on Multiple Paths**\nThe branch maintains tunnels to six hubs. **Two tunnels show significantly elevated loss & jitter**:\n\n| Tunnel | Latency (ms) | Jitter (ms) | Loss (%) | Rekeys |\n|--------|-------------|-------------|----------|--------|\n| ce_branch24-ce_hub1 | 71.7 | 3.8 | **2.77** | 4 |\n| ce_branch24-ce_hub2 | 63.6 | 1.2 | **4.76** | **16** |\n| ce_branch24-ce_hub3 | 72.3 | 4.4 | 0.05 | **25** |\n| ce_branch24-ce_hub4 | 65.9 | 6.6 | 0.13 | 4 |\n| ce_branch24-ce_hub5 | 63.0 | 7.4 | 0.11 | 4 |\n| ce_branch24-ce_hub6 | 70.9 | 6.8 | 0.08 | 4 |\n\n**Key findings** [metrics:6-17][metrics:18-23]:\n- **ce_hub1 & ce_hub2 paths have loss > 2.5 %** \u2014 well above typical SLA thresholds (\u2264 1 %).\n- **ce_hub2 shows 16 rekeys** (vs. 4 on most others), indicating frequent tunnel renegotiation / instability.\n- **ce_hub3 shows 25 rekeys** despite low loss \u2014 possible MTU / fragmentation or crypto mismatch.\n- Jitter on ce_hub4/5/6 (6\u20137 ms) is elevated for a branch link.\n\n## Local Interface Counters\n- **eth0 (primary WAN?)**: 9.9 MB in / 3.8 MB out, **1 877 input discards**, **90 queue drops** [metrics:6][metrics:8][metrics:17][metrics:26].\n- **eth1**: light traffic, 2 queue drops [metrics:7][metrics:9][metrics:18].\n- **wg0 (WireGuard overlay)**: ~940 kB in / 961 kB out, no errors/discards [metrics:16][metrics:25].\n- **VRF CORP & VOICE**: inbound traffic only (56 kB / 54 kB), **zero outbound** [metrics:14][metrics:15][metrics:23][metrics:24] \u2014 suggests asymmetric routing or firewall policy dropping return traffic.\n\n## Topology Blast-Radius (2 hops) [topo:ce_branch24]\n- **Upstream**: pe12 (core PE) \u2014 healthy, BGP established, MPLS LDP up, OSPF full.\n- **Downstream hosts**: h_branch24_corp, h_branch24_voice \u2014 no metrics visible (likely end-hosts).\n- **Sibling branches**: ce_branch12 (2 hops via pe12) \u2014 healthy, loss 0.12 %, latency 58 ms.\n- **Core P-routers**: p23, p24 \u2014 healthy.\n\n## Overall Assessment\n**ce_branch24 is operationally up but experiencing WAN-quality degradation on at least two of six hub tunnels (ce_hub1, ce_hub2)**, plus frequent rekeys on ce_hub2/ce_hub3. The 1 877 input discards and 90 queue drops on eth0 coincide with the high-loss tunnels, pointing to **congestion or policing on the primary WAN interface (eth0)**. VRF egress silence (CORP/VOICE) warrants a policy/ACL check.\n\n## Recommended Next Steps\n1. **Capture a ranged metric series** for `sdwan_tunnel_loss_pct`/`jitter_ms` on ce_hub1/ce_hub2 over the last 30\u201360 min to confirm trend.\n2. **Check eth0 speed/duplex & QoS policy** \u2014 90 queue drops + 1 877 discards suggest tail-drop or policer.\n3. **Verify MTU / PMTU** on ce_hub3 path (high rekeys, low loss).\n4. **Inspect VRF CORP/VOICE egress ACLs / firewall rules** on ce_branch24 and upstream pe12.\n5. **Correlate with ISP / underlay monitoring** for the circuits terminating on eth0."}

